---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/FlowIcon.astro';
import ScrollConnections from '../components/ScrollConnections.astro';
import FieldNotesPreview from '../components/FieldNotesPreview.astro';
import RequirementsExample from '../components/RequirementsExample.astro';
import { wanderAppStoreUrl, wanderWebsiteUrl } from '../lib/site-links';
import '../styles/visual-home.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Hyphos: Your Best People Have Better Things To Do" description="Less chasing information. Less entering it twice. Hyphos connects the knowledge behind your work, with people providing judgment where it matters.">
<div class="visual-page v-dark">
  <section class="v-hero v-shell">
    <p class="v-eyebrow">Hyphos Inc. · Software &amp; Knowledge Platform</p>
    <h1>Your Best People<br /><em>Have Better Things To Do</em></h1>
    <p class="v-intro">Less chasing information. Less entering it twice. Less explaining it again.</p>
    <p class="v-hero-context">What did we quote? What did the job actually take? What does the contract require? Hyphos connects your estimates, invoices, timesheets, emails and documents, and on larger work the contracts and requirements behind them, so your team can see what needs doing, and why.</p>
    <div class="v-actions"><a href="#how-it-works" class="button button--gold">See How It Works ↓</a><a href="#field-notes" class="text-link">Explore The Field Notes ↓</a></div>
    <details class="v-detail"><summary>What Is Hyphos?</summary><div><p>Hyphos connects the information scattered across a business: estimates and invoices, timesheets and supplier bills, accounting, emails, documents, meetings and AI conversations. On larger engagements it also connects contracts, scopes of work and regulations.</p><p>Those relationships help your team catch a gap before it costs money, understand the effect of a change and trace a decision back to its sources. We’re open to design partners who want to shape it around a real workflow. <a href="/pricing">See what a pilot involves ↗</a></p></div></details>
  </section>
  <!-- The question every visitor is already asking, answered in four lines.
       Depth lives in the field note, not here. -->
  <section id="the-wall" class="v-chapter v-wall"><div class="v-shell">
    <div class="v-chapter-heading">
      <p class="v-eyebrow">The Question We Get Most</p>
      <h2>Why Not Just Ask<br /><em>Claude Or ChatGPT?</em></h2>
      <p class="v-wall-lead">For one meeting or one document, go ahead. We use them every day. The trouble starts when there is a lot of material.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="v-wall-list">
      <li><strong>It answers from memory, not from your file. “Hallucination”</strong> It keeps a piece of what it read, fills in the rest, and believes the result. It will not go back and check unless you tell it to.</li>
      <li><strong>It misses what you changed.</strong> You decided something, then changed it. It answers with the old decision.</li>
      <li><strong>It cannot check its own work.</strong> Ask it to double check and it agrees with itself.</li>
      <li><strong>It says it read everything.</strong> We gave one twelve hours of meetings. It reported back done. It had skimmed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="v-wall-close">A better prompt does not fix this. Every answer has to stay tied to the document it came from, get checked against that document automatically, and be counted, so you can see what was actually read and what was not.</p>
    <div class="v-wall-cta"><a href="/field-notes/it-said-it-read-everything/" class="button button--gold">See How This Goes Wrong ↗</a></div>
  </div></section>

  <ScrollConnections />
  <section id="client-example" class="v-chapter v-light-chapter"><div class="v-shell">
    <div class="v-chapter-heading"><p class="v-eyebrow">02 · From A Small Job To A Large Engagement</p><h2>What Was Agreed<br />What It Actually Took<br /><em>What Needs Doing</em></h2><p>A one-week job or a year-long engagement, the gap shows up the same way: the pieces sit in different places. Hyphos brings them into view, with the source behind each one.</p></div>
    <RequirementsExample />
    <details class="v-detail"><summary>What Happens When A Job Runs Over?</summary><div><p>The estimate, the hours, the supplier bills and the invoice stay connected to the job, so the difference shows up before the invoice goes out, not after the customer has paid.</p><p>Your team still decides what to bill. The numbers, and where each one came from, are in front of them when they do.</p></div></details>
    <details class="v-detail"><summary>What Happens When A Requirement Changes?</summary><div><p>The next question is which commitments, scope items, tasks and records depend on it. Hyphos is designed to carry those relationships with the information, so your team can see what needs another look.</p><p>The source stays available alongside the work. People can check applicability, resolve conflicting obligations and review the proposed change with the relevant evidence in view.</p><p><a href="/field-notes/which-document-can-you-trust/">Read the field note: what does this work need to satisfy? ↗</a></p></div></details>
  </div></section>
  <section class="v-chapter"><div class="v-shell">
    <div class="v-chapter-heading"><p class="v-eyebrow">03 · Carry It Forward</p><h2>New Person<br /><em>Same Understanding</em></h2></div>
    <figure>
      <div class="v-handoff"><div class="v-person"><Icon name="people" /><span>Today’s team</span></div><div class="v-task"><p>Next step · Office manager</p><h3>Invoice The Bathroom Renovation</h3><ul><li><Icon name="invoice" />Estimate: accepted, 32 hours</li><li><Icon name="payroll" />Timesheets: 38 hours logged</li><li><Icon name="scope" />Open: approve 6 extra hours</li></ul></div><div class="v-person"><Icon name="people" /><span>The next person</span></div></div>
      <figcaption class="v-caption" style="text-align:center">Illustrative handoff · Sample content</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <details class="v-detail"><summary>What Changes At The Handoff?</summary><div><p>Whoever picks the work up, the office manager covering a vacation or the next consultant on an engagement, can see what was agreed, the numbers or the scope, the sources and the work still to do, without asking someone to reconstruct every conversation.</p><p>Hyphos supports their judgment; the team remains responsible for reviewing and carrying out the work.</p></div></details>
    <div class="v-work-links"><a href="/architecture" class="text-link">Explore How Hyphos Is Designed ↗</a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section id="domas" class="v-chapter v-domas"><div class="v-shell">
    <div class="v-chapter-heading"><p class="v-eyebrow">Domas · How Hyphos Gets Built</p><h2>A System That<br /><em>Builds Itself</em></h2><p>Most software waits on a team of programmers. We built Domas instead: AI plans each change to Hyphos, builds it, tests it and checks the work, and a person approves it along the way.</p></div>
    <figure>
      <div class="v-domas-flow"><div class="v-business-needs"><div><Icon name="ai" /><span>A New Idea</span></div><div><Icon name="check" /><span>A Problem To Fix</span></div><div><Icon name="people" /><span>A Change Someone Asked For</span></div></div><div class="v-domas-core"><strong>Domas</strong><span aria-label="turns it into">→</span></div><div class="v-tailored"><p>Inside Domas</p><h3>Plan, Build, Check</h3><ol><li><span>01</span>AI Writes The Plan</li><li><span>02</span>A Person Approves It</li><li><span>03</span>AI Builds And Tests It</li><li><span>04</span>A Second AI Reviews The Work</li></ol></div></div>
      <figcaption class="v-caption" style="text-align:center">How Hyphos is built today · A person approves every plan before the work starts</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p class="v-domas-loop">Idea → Plan → Approve → Build → Test → Review ↻</p>
    <details class="v-detail"><summary>What Does “Builds Itself” Actually Mean?</summary><div><p>Think of Domas as a small software team made of AI, run by a manager who never skips the paperwork. It writes down the plan, builds the change in a separate copy so nothing live is touched, runs the tests and has a different AI check the result. Every decision is recorded, so the next change starts from what was already learned.</p><p>It does not run unsupervised. A named person approves each plan before any building starts, and the work is reviewed before it becomes part of Hyphos. That is how one small team can build and change a large system quickly without losing track of it.</p><p>What’s next: using the same system to shape Hyphos around each business, its terms, steps and tools, with that business approving the changes. That part is still being built.</p><p><a href="/architecture#domas">Explore Domas and the architecture ↗</a></p></div></details>
  </div></section>
  <section id="selected-work" class="v-chapter v-proof v-light-chapter"><div class="v-shell">
    <div class="v-chapter-heading"><p class="v-eyebrow">Built By Hyphos</p><h2>Behind The Website<br /><em>A Connected Business</em></h2><p>We also build software for clients. The same idea runs through it: record information once, and use it where it belongs.</p></div>
    <div class="v-proof-display">
      <figure><div class="v-portal-frame"><img src="/work/cornerstone/staff-portal.png" width="2912" height="2340" alt="Actual client staff portal, showing its calendar and business navigation" loading="lazy" /></div><figcaption class="v-caption">Actual client software · Staff portal</figcaption></figure>
      <div class="v-proof-points"><div class="v-proof-point"><Icon name="people" /><div><strong>The Team</strong><span>Records &amp; daily work</span></div></div><div class="v-proof-point"><Icon name="website" /><div><strong>The Customer</strong><span>Website &amp; publishing</span></div></div><div class="v-proof-point"><Icon name="insight" /><div><strong>The Next Decision</strong><span>Marketing &amp; reporting</span></div></div></div>
    </div>
    <details class="v-detail"><summary>See How The Pieces Connect</summary><div><p>For client Cornerstone Funeral Home, service records can supply website content. The public site reads published information, while website activity and available marketing signals feed staff reporting.</p><p><a href="/work/cornerstone">Explore the connected software ↗</a></p></div></details>
    <div class="v-work-links"><a href="/work" class="text-link">See All Our Work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="v-chapter v-wander v-light-chapter"><div class="v-shell">
    <div class="v-chapter-heading"><p class="v-eyebrow">Client Work · iPhone &amp; Android Apps</p><h2>From An Idea<br /><em>To The App Store</em></h2><p>Wander is a consumer app we designed, built and shipped to the App Store from a single codebase that also builds the Android app. It’s a full production product, with maps, real-time messaging, AI-powered search, camera and location features and push notifications, not a prototype or a website in an app shell.</p></div>
    <ol class="v-app-steps"><li><span>01</span>Designed</li><li><span>02</span>Built</li><li><span>03</span>Tested</li><li><span>04</span>Approved By Apple</li><li><span>05</span>Live On The App Store</li></ol>
    <div class="v-wander-shots"><img src="/work/wander/wander-find.webp" width="640" height="1388" alt="Wander, a client app, showing its map of nearby parks" loading="lazy" /><img src="/work/wander/wander-check.webp" width="640" height="1388" alt="Wander place details with photos, reviews and amenities" loading="lazy" /><img src="/work/wander/wander-go.webp" width="640" height="1388" alt="Wander outing plan to share with friends" loading="lazy" /></div>
    <div class="v-actions"><a href={wanderAppStoreUrl} class="button button--gold" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See It On The App Store <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/work#wander" class="text-link">How We Built It <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="v-chapter"><div class="v-shell">
    <div class="v-chapter-heading"><p class="v-eyebrow">Where We Can Help</p><h2>Start Where The Work<br /><em>Gets Stuck</em></h2></div>
    <div class="v-capabilities"><article><Icon name="records" /><h3>Connect Your Systems</h3><p>Less copying. Fewer gaps.</p></article><article><Icon name="website" /><h3>Build The Missing Piece</h3><p>Software and apps that fit the work.</p></article><article><Icon name="people" /><h3>Put Knowledge To Work</h3><p>Practical AI on your own information.</p></article></div>
    <div class="v-work-links"><a href="/services" class="text-link">Explore Our Services <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </div></section>
  <FieldNotesPreview />
  <section class="v-closing v-shell"><p class="v-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:20px">Start Small</p><h2>Does This Happen<br /><em>In Your Business?</em></h2><p>A question is enough. There’s no need for a prepared brief.</p><div class="v-actions"><a href="mailto:info@hyphos.io?subject=A%20question%20about%20Hyphos" class="button button--gold">Ask Us A Question ↗</a><a href="/contact" class="text-link">Talk With Us ↗</a></div><p>Opens your email app.</p></section>
</div>

<style>
.v-wall{background:#15171a;border-top:1px solid #ffffff1f;border-bottom:1px solid #ffffff1f;}
.v-wall .v-chapter-heading{text-align:center;}
.v-wall-lead{max-width:60ch;margin:0 auto;font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.7;color:#c9cace;}
.v-wall-list{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:40px auto 0;max-width:1000px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:14px 28px;}
.v-wall-list li{border-left:2px solid #b69259;padding:4px 0 4px 16px;font-size:1.0625rem;line-height:1.6;color:#b9babd;}
.v-wall-list strong{display:block;color:#f1efe2;font-weight:600;}
.v-wall-close{max-width:70ch;margin:40px auto 0;text-align:center;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.75;color:#c9cace;}
.v-wall-cta{margin-top:30px;text-align:center;}
.v-wall-cta .button{font-size:1.05rem;padding:15px 30px;}
@media(max-width:760px){.v-wall-list{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px;}.v-wall-lead{font-size:1.05rem;}}
</style>
</BaseLayout>
